{"id":"330c17cc-0fff-4c7e-a017-6432f9bcfc47","object":"chat.completion","created":1789626563,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need answer only JSON. Need solve. Need produce complete program satisfying policy. We have feedback. Need synthesize select and step rules at most 12 each, total branches <=32. Need ensure all 32 select inputs, all mode*step facts covered. Need expressions only permitted booleans, not comparisons. Need one-hot mode flags exactly one true. Step cannot use select names. Select cannot use step/mode names.\n\nWe need understand policy fully. Previous candidate had issues:\n- step stop rule split wrong: first \"not Obs... or ...\" action Brake next Stopped, second same next BrakeRequested. First matches all invalid including Halted false, so incorrect. Need condition for invalid/blocked: action Brake, next Stopped if Halted true, next BrakeRequested otherwise. So two rules:\n  invalid/blocked and Halted -> Brake, Stopped\n  invalid/blocked and not Halted -> Brake, BrakeRequested\nPriority highest. Or one rule can't conditional next. Need two rules. But note Halted true? Policy: highest condition whenever invalid/blocked/task inactive, return Brake. Under that, enter Stopped if Halted true and BrakeRequested otherwise. Yes.\n\n- missing ordinary Proceed fallback. Previous no default, caused undefined. Need add default Proceed Traversing after all priority rules.\n\nNeed carefully order all step rules according to authority:\n1. invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling highest.\n   - if (not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted -> Brake, Stopped.\n   - if (not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted -> Brake, BrakeRequested.\n   Order between these no overlap if Halted true/false.\n2. released-goal handling: AtGoal and Released both true:\n   - without Halted: Brake, BrakeRequested.\n   - with Halted: Finish, Done.\n   Need priority within released-goal? \"without Halted, return Brake...; with Halted, return Finish...\" If Halted true finish; if false brake. Could order Halted finish then not Halted brake. Both cover AtGoal & Released. Must be after invalid highest, so if invalid and AtGoal Released Halted true, invalid rule catches first (Brake Stopped? Wait highest invalid says Brake, next Stopped if Halted true. So yes invalid overrides finish). Then AtGoal Released Halted -> Finish Done.\n   Need condition \"AtGoal and Released and Halted\" -> Finish Done.\n   \"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\" -> Brake BrakeRequested. (If Halted false)\n3. whole-body release: OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ -> Release, Traversing. This is higher than unfinished braking. Need after released-goal? Authority order: invalid/blocked/task-inactive; released-goal; whole-body release; unfinished braking; reservation request; restart transition; ordinary motion. Yes.\n   Condition OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ. Does it require TaskActive etc? Not stated. If invalid, invalid catches. If AtGoal Released, released-goal catches before. Note if OwnReservation BodyClearOfZ AtGoal Released Halted true, released-goal Finish wins over Release. If AtGoal Released not Halted, Brake wins.\n4. unfinished braking: \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides missing-reservation request.\" Does this apply only current ModeBrakeRequested? Wording: \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested\" likely current mode is BrakeRequested and not Halted. Step inputs don't include separate BrakeRequested fact except mode flag. So condition ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted -> Brake, BrakeRequested. Need after release. Note if OwnReservation BodyClearOfZ and ModeBrakeRequested not Halted: whole-body release overrides unfinished braking per order? They specified \"However, OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\" Yes release before.\n5. reservation request: \"A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides the restart transition. BrakeRequested without Halted ... overrides a missing-reservation request.\" So rule after unfinished braking: not OwnReservation and not Released -> Request Waiting. Does this apply any mode? Yes. If mode BrakeRequested and not Halted, previous catches even if missing reservation. If invalid/goal/release catch earlier. Condition no OwnReservation and no Released. \"missing reservation requires Request\" Perhaps also should not apply if AtGoal? But released-goal only if AtGoal & Released. If AtGoal true and Released false, missing reservation? Policy: AtGoal with Released true triggers; otherwise missing reservation may require Request? Need examine. AtGoal false? If at goal but not released? Actually AtGoal and Released both true arrival handling. If AtGoal true but Released false, Released false so missing reservation condition true (not OwnReservation and not Released) maybe request. Policy says missing reservation requires Request when neither OwnReservation nor Released true. It does not exclude AtGoal. Since Released false means not acknowledged release. Could be task active at goal awaiting release. Yes request? Odd but policy explicit. Higher authority released-goal only AtGoal and Released both true. So okay.\n6. restart transition: \"applies to a current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending. A missing reservation ... overrides restart transition. ... BrakeRequested ... overrides missing-reservation.\" So condition ModeStopped -> Resume, ResumePending. After reservation request. Note if Stopped and missing reservation, request catches. If Stopped and BrakeRequested? Current mode exactly one, can't both. If OwnReservation BodyClearOfZ, release catches before. If AtGoal Released Halted finish catches. If invalid catches.\n7. ordinary motion: Proceed entering Traversing. This is fallback for remaining valid input. Need condition True -> Proceed, Traversing. Must be last. Does ordinary outcome apply even if ModeStopped but OwnReservation something? Wait restart applies ModeStopped -> Resume. So if ModeStopped and not missing reservation, not release, not invalid, not goal, it resumes. If ModeStopped and OwnReservation true BodyClearOfZ false Released true, restart -> Resume. Is that correct? Authority: restart transition lower than missing reservation. Released true means missing reservation false. So restart. Yes.\n\nNeed consider ModeBrakeRequested and Halted true. Unfinished braking only without Halted. Then what? If Halted true, maybe if missing reservation -> Request; if ModeStopped? No. If not missing, maybe ordinary Proceed Traversing. Is that correct? Policy: \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake...\"; with Halted, no unfinished braking. If no higher obligation, ordinary Proceed. But could be weird: mode BrakeRequested, Halted true, Task active, observation usable, no reservation -> missing reservation Request Waiting (if neither own nor released) even though halted. If OwnReservation true Released false, no request, proceed Traversing. Is that intended? Need rely on policy. It says these rules apply every mode, if multiple descriptions use higher. Restart transition only Stopped. So yes.\n\nNeed select. Previous select:\nOwnerFree and RequestA and RequestB -> SelectA\nOwnerFree and RequestA -> SelectA\nOwnerFree and RequestB -> SelectB\nTrue -> Defer\nNeed verify select policy: Selecting A requires OwnerFree and RequestA; selecting B requires OwnerFree and RequestB. If reservation free and at least one request exists, select eligible robot rather than Defer. Otherwise Defer required. When both eligible, either legal; preferences no additional acceptance obligation. So this works? For OwnerFree true RequestA true RequestB false: third not match, second match SelectA. For OwnerFree true RequestA false RequestB true: first false, second false, third SelectB. For both true: first SelectA. For OwnerFree false any: True Defer. Good.\nNeed maybe preferences can be ignored. At most 12. Good.\n\nNeed produce JSON. But we need ensure no duplicate keys, exact keys. Step rules ordered.\n\nLet's craft step rules list:\n\n[\n{\"when\":\"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"Stopped\"}? Need include Halted for Stopped. Let's define:\n1. {\"when\":\"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"Stopped\"}\n2. {\"when\":\"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"BrakeRequested\"}\n3. {\"when\":\"AtGoal and Released and Halted\",\"action\":\"Finish\",\"next\":\"Done\"}\n4. {\"when\":\"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"BrakeRequested\"}\n5. {\"when\":\"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\",\"action\":\"Release\",\"next\":\"Traversing\"}\n6. {\"when\":\"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"BrakeRequested\"}\n7. {\"when\":\"not OwnReservation and not Released\",\"action\":\"Request\",\"next\":\"Waiting\"}\n8. {\"when\":\"ModeStopped\",\"action\":\"Resume\",\"next\":\"ResumePending\"}\n9. {\"when\":\"True\",\"action\":\"Proceed\",\"next\":\"Traversing\"}\n]\n\nNeed check rule 1/2 expression syntax: parentheses allowed. Need expression chars <=512, depth <=8. okay. But operator precedence: not > and > or. Parentheses fine.\nPotential issue: In rule 1, condition invalid and Halted. If invalid and Halted true, action Brake next Stopped. Policy says under highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted true and BrakeRequested otherwise. Yes.\n\nPotential issue: \"released-goal handling\" says \"Higher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done.\" It says Higher than all these (whole-body release etc). We put after invalid. Good. But within released-goal, if AtGoal and Released and Halted true -> Finish; if false -> Brake. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"whole-body release\" condition OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release. What if AtGoal and Released false, OwnReservation true BodyClearOfZ true? Released false means missing reservation? Wait condition \"missing reservation when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true.\" If OwnReservation true, missing reservation false, so Release rule catches. Good. If AtGoal true Released false OwnReservation true BodyClearOfZ true, release rule catches. Is that okay? Released-goal only AtGoal & Released both. So yes Release.\n\nPotential issue: \"A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides the restart transition.\" Our rule 7 condition not OwnReservation and not Released. It doesn't include TaskActive etc. Invalid catches if task inactive. AtGoal and Released false, OwnReservation false -> Request. Yes.\n\nPotential issue: \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request.\" Our rule 6 catches ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted, before rule 7. Yes. But what about invalid condition and ModeBrakeRequested not Halted? Rule 2 catches if invalid and not Halted -> Brake BrakeRequested. Same action/next as rule 6, so no issue. If invalid and Halted true, rule1 catches Brake Stopped vs rule6 not (Halted true). Good.\nPotential issue: \"BrakeRequested without Halted\" might mean input fact? There is no BrakeRequested fact, only mode. So okay.\n\nPotential issue: \"restart transition applies to a current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending.\" Our rule 8 catches all ModeStopped not caught earlier. For ModeStopped and missing reservation, rule7 catches Request Waiting. For ModeStopped and invalid, rule1/2 catch Brake. For ModeStopped and AtGoal Released Halted -> Finish. For ModeStopped and AtGoal Released not Halted -> Brake. For ModeStopped and OwnReservation BodyClearOfZ -> Release Traversing. For ModeStopped and ModeBrakeRequested can't both. So correct.\n\nPotential issue: ordinary step outcome is Proceed entering Traversing. It is displaced by requirements. Our fallback True covers all remaining. Good.\n\nNeed maybe \"select\" expressions cannot use mode names, okay. Step expressions cannot use select names, okay.\n\nNeed output exactly JSON object no markdown. We can include spaces. Must be valid UTF-8. Ensure no duplicate keys. Root exactly schema, select, step. Each rule select has exactly when action. Step has when action next. At most 12. Total branches? 4 select + 9 step = 13. Good.\n\nBut wait: The diagnostic says previous candidate had model_violation for invalid/Halted false: actual [\"Brake\",\"Stopped\"], allowed [\"Brake\",\"BrakeRequested\"]. Our new fixes.\n\nNeed consider if we need <12 step, okay.\n\nLet's think if there are hidden pitfalls. The policy \"invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling; released-goal handling; whole-body release; unfinished braking; reservation request; restart transition; ordinary motion.\" It might require invalid handling condition: \"whenever ObservationUsable is false, TaskActive is false, or PedestrianBlocked is true, return Brake. Under that highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted is true and BrakeRequested otherwise.\" We did.\n\nWhat about if invalid and Halted true but current mode Done? Policy applies every mode including Done. We did.\n\nWhat about \"AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done.\" If invalid also true, invalid highest. We did.\n\nWhat about \"whole-body release\" if invalid? invalid higher. If AtGoal Released? released-goal higher. If ModeBrakeRequested not Halted? release higher per \"before unfinished braking\". We did. But what about missing reservation? release condition OwnReservation true so missing reservation false. Good.\n\nWhat about \"unfinished braking\" priority relative to reservation request. We did. \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request.\" We did. But what if ModeBrakeRequested and Halted false and OwnReservation false Released false. Rule6 catches, so Request not. Good. If ModeBrakeRequested and Halted false and AtGoal Released true, rule4 catches Brake BrakeRequested (same action/next). If AtGoal Released and Halted true, rule3 Finish Done, but rule6 doesn't because Halted true. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\" If ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted and OwnReservation BodyClearOfZ true, rule5 Release Traversing catches, overriding unfinished braking. We did. Is that correct? Yes. But wait, if current mode BrakeRequested and not Halted, \"unfinished braking must continue Brake\" but exception: OwnReservation BodyClearOfZ requires Release before unfinished braking. So release wins. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"missing reservation\" condition \"neither OwnReservation nor Released is true\" - Should it also require not AtGoal? If AtGoal true Released false, OwnReservation false, Request. Is that physically odd but policy. The diagnostic examples might include? The previous candidate didn't have Proceed fallback, but had reservation request before restart. It might have matched some. Need maybe check if policy expects no Request if AtGoal? Let's parse original: \"The restart transition applies to a current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending. A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides the restart transition. BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request. However, OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\n\nHigher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done. Highest of all, whenever ObservationUsable is false, TaskActive is false, or PedestrianBlocked is true, return Brake. Under that highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted is true and BrakeRequested otherwise.\"\n\nThus order: highest invalid; then arrival AtGoal & Released; then OwnReservation & BodyClearOfZ; then unfinished braking; then missing reservation; then restart; then ordinary. Yes.\n\nBut wait, the list authority says: \"invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling; released-goal handling; whole-body release; unfinished braking; reservation request; restart transition; ordinary motion.\" Yes matches.\n\nNeed maybe \"AtGoal and Released both true\" released-goal handling is higher than whole-body release. We did.\n\nPotential issue: \"with Halted, return Finish and enter Done\" for AtGoal&Released. But invalid highest: if AtGoal Released Halted and invalid, invalid returns Brake Stopped. But what if invalid and Halted false, invalid returns Brake BrakeRequested same as AtGoal without Halted. So okay.\n\nPotential issue: \"TaskActive is false\" invalid. Suppose TaskActive false, Halted true. Our rule1 Brake Stopped. Policy says under highest condition, enter Stopped if Halted true. Yes. But is \"Brake\" appropriate even if already Stopped? Yes.\n\nPotential issue: \"PedestrianBlocked true\" invalid. If Halted true, Brake Stopped. Yes.\n\nPotential issue: The step inputs include \"Released\" distinct from BodyClearOfZ. We used.\n\nPotential issue: \"Halted is a trusted stop confirmation, not merely the issuance of a Brake command.\" We used.\n\nPotential issue: \"AtGoal and TaskActive have literal task meanings.\" We used.\n\nPotential issue: \"Do not infer relationships between Boolean inputs beyond one-hot mode flags.\" Our expressions don't.\n\nPotential issue: \"The generated program cannot alter these facts.\" Fine.\n\nPotential issue: \"No special terminal-mode shortcut exists: requirements apply in every mode, including Done.\" We have no special Done.\n\nPotential issue: \"All 32 combinations of select facts and all 7 * 256 combinations of mode and step facts are evaluated, even combinations not physically reachable.\" We cover all via True fallback. Need ensure every mode one-hot. Our rules don't require mode except ModeBrakeRequested and ModeStopped. Fallback covers. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"At most 32 total branches allowed; per-function limit 12 still applies.\" We have 13.\n\nPotential issue: Source size <=200KB. tiny.\n\nPotential issue: \"Duplicate JSON keys rejected.\" No.\n\nPotential issue: \"A condition has at most 512 characters, 64 Python syntax-tree nodes and expression depth eight.\" Our longest condition \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\" okay. Nodes maybe: not Obs (2), or not Task (2), or Ped (1), and not Halted (2) plus parentheses. <64.\n\nNeed decide whether to use \"not ObservationUsable\" or \"ObservationUsable == False\"? Only allowed not. We use not.\n\nNeed maybe use capital True/False. Yes.\n\nNeed maybe root order? JSON order doesn't matter but we can schema, select, step. The instruction says root exactly three keys: \"schema\", \"select\", \"step\". It might not require order, but we can follow. Duplicate keys no. Output exactly one JSON object.\n\nLet's consider if select should handle preferences? The interface: \"PreferA/PreferB are advisory. Selecting A requires OwnerFree and RequestA; selecting B requires OwnerFree and RequestB. If a reservation is free and at least one request exists, select an eligible robot, rather than Defer. Otherwise Defer is required. When both robots are eligible, either is legal; preferences do not impose an additional acceptance obligation, and their values may conflict or both be absent.\" Our select ignores Prefer. When both eligible, SelectA legal. When only A, SelectA. When only B, SelectB. When none, Defer. When OwnerFree false, Defer. Good. Could there be condition OwnerFree true, RequestA false, RequestB true, PreferA true? Our SelectB. Legal. Good.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"select inputs: OwnerFree, RequestA, RequestB, PreferA, PreferB.\" \"If a reservation is free and at least one request exists, select an eligible robot, rather than Defer.\" If OwnerFree true and both RequestA and RequestB false, Defer. Our True Defer catches. If OwnerFree true RequestA true RequestB false, SelectA. If OwnerFree true RequestA false RequestB true, SelectB. If both true, SelectA. Good.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"When both robots are eligible, either is legal; preferences do not impose an additional acceptance obligation\" Could they require that preferences can break ties? No, advisory. Our choice A regardless preferences. Legal.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"Selecting A requires OwnerFree and RequestA; selecting B requires OwnerFree and RequestB.\" Our first rule OwnerFree and RequestA and RequestB -> SelectA. Satisfies. Second OwnerFree and RequestA -> SelectA. If both true, first matches. If only A, second. Third OwnerFree and RequestB -> SelectB. If both true, first prevents third. If only B, third. Good.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"Every possible input must have a result.\" Select True Defer. Step True Proceed. Good.\n\nLet's maybe check step coverage for a tricky combo: ModeIdle, invalid false, AtGoal true Released true Halted false, OwnReservation true BodyClearOfZ true. Rule4 (AtGoal Released not Halted) -> Brake BrakeRequested. Policy: released-goal higher than whole-body release. Yes. If Halted true, rule3 Finish Done. Good.\nModeIdle, invalid false, AtGoal false Released true, OwnReservation true BodyClearOfZ true. Rule5 Release Traversing. Is this correct? Authority: whole-body release before unfinished etc. Released true means not missing reservation. So release. But what does Released mean? \"Released denotes an acknowledged reservation release for its task; it is distinct from BodyClearOfZ.\" If Released true, why would OwnReservation true? Could be physically impossible but evaluated. Policy says if OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ requires Release. So yes.\nModeIdle, invalid false, AtGoal false Released false, OwnReservation true BodyClearOfZ false. Rule7? not OwnReservation false, so no. Rule8? ModeIdle no. Fallback Proceed Traversing. Is that correct? Missing reservation condition false because OwnReservation true. No release because BodyClearOfZ false. No braking, restart. So ordinary Proceed. Yes.\nModeIdle, invalid false, AtGoal false Released false, OwnReservation false BodyClearOfZ true. Rule7 missing reservation -> Request Waiting. Because neither OwnReservation nor Released. BodyClearOfZ irrelevant. Yes.\nModeStopped, invalid false, AtGoal false Released false, OwnReservation false BodyClearOfZ true. Rule7 missing reservation -> Request Waiting, overrides restart. Yes.\nModeStopped, invalid false, AtGoal false Released true, OwnReservation false BodyClearOfZ true. Rule7 false (Released true). Rule8 ModeStopped -> Resume ResumePending. Is that correct? Missing reservation false because Released true. Restart transition applies. Yes.\nModeStopped, invalid false, AtGoal false Released false, OwnReservation true BodyClearOfZ true. Rule5 Release Traversing. It overrides restart? Authority: whole-body release higher than reservation request and restart. Yes. Wait missing reservation false because OwnReservation true, but release. So Release Traversing instead of restart. Is that intended? \"OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\" It is above unfinished braking, reservation request, restart. So yes.\nModeBrakeRequested, invalid false, AtGoal false Released false, OwnReservation false BodyClearOfZ false Halted false. Rule6 Brake BrakeRequested. It overrides missing-reservation request. Yes.\nModeBrakeRequested, invalid false, AtGoal false Released false, OwnReservation false BodyClearOfZ false Halted true. Rule6 false. Rule7 missing reservation -> Request Waiting. Is that correct? \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake... overrides missing-reservation.\" With Halted true, missing reservation overrides? Then Request. Yes.\nModeBrakeRequested, invalid false, AtGoal true Released true Halted true. Rule3 Finish Done. But current mode BrakeRequested, Halted true. Policy: released-goal higher than unfinished braking. Yes. If invalid also true, invalid higher. Good.\nModeDone, invalid false, AtGoal false Released false, OwnReservation false BodyClearOfZ false. Rule7 missing reservation -> Request Waiting even in Done. Policy says no terminal shortcut. Yes. If OwnReservation true Released true, fallback Proceed Traversing from Done? Wait ModeDone, no special. AtGoal false Released true OwnReservation true BodyClearOfZ false. Rules: invalid false; goal false; release false (BodyClear false); unfinished false (not ModeBrakeRequested); missing false (OwnReservation true); restart false; fallback Proceed Traversing. So Done can transition to Traversing. Is that required? \"No special terminal-mode shortcut exists: requirements apply in every mode, including Done.\" Ordinary step outcome is Proceed entering Traversing unless displaced. So yes.\n\nPotential hidden issue: The policy says \"The ordinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing. It is displaced by the following requirements.\" Does ordinary outcome apply regardless current mode? Yes. So Done can Proceed. Good.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"restart transition applies to a current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending.\" If current Stopped and no other obligations, Resume. Our rule8. If current Stopped and invalid, Brake. If missing, Request. If release, Release. If goal, Finish/Brake. If ModeBrakeRequested can't. Good.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides the restart transition.\" Does this apply even when AtGoal and Released false? We said yes. Let's double-check: AtGoal true Released false means Released not true, so missing reservation condition true if OwnReservation false. It would Request Waiting. But maybe \"released-goal handling\" only AtGoal and Released both true; if AtGoal true Released false, perhaps still missing reservation. The policy's authority order includes reservation request lower than released-goal but higher than restart. So yes.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"released-goal handling\" maybe if AtGoal true and Released false, should it maybe be part of released-goal handling? It says \"Higher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake...; with Halted, return Finish...\" If AtGoal true but Released false, not arrival with both. So no.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\" Does it require OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ and maybe not Released? No. We use exactly.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested\" Could \"BrakeRequested\" refer to current mode? The mode names include ModeBrakeRequested. The step inputs do not include BrakeRequested fact. So yes. They might phrase \"BrakeRequested\" as mode. We use ModeBrakeRequested.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"Halted is a trusted stop confirmation, not merely issuance of Brake command.\" We 